WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.875
The lab runs in a test tenant, never
production, and the authors haven't run it.

2
00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:09.715
You need Module 2's lab done, the emergency
access group, a tenant restrictions

3
00:00:09.715 --> 00:00:13.950
policy with one allowed partner,
and test accounts in three tenants.

4
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.525
Step one confirms signaling and reads
the compliant network named location.

5
00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:22.200
Step two finds the two Intune
applications to exclude.

6
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.713
Step three creates the pilot policy in
report-only, with the guide's exact body.

7
00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:31.212
Step four reads the would-be
blocks in the workspace.

8
00:00:31.212 --> 00:00:35.441
The guide reads them for ten business
days; a report-only failure from a

9
00:00:35.441 --> 00:00:39.962
sign-in that came through the service
is a defect to fix before enforcement.

10
00:00:39.962 --> 00:00:44.074
In a test tenant the lab shortens
that; in production, never.

11
00:00:44.074 --> 00:00:46.125
Step five proves the block.

12
00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:51.018
Confirm your emergency access account
isn't in the pilot, set the policy on, and

13
00:00:51.018 --> 00:00:56.063
on the pilot device disable the client and
sign in again in a new browser session.

14
00:00:56.063 --> 00:01:00.960
Expect "You can't access this right now."
Then put the policy back in report-only.
